! double_gyre_unsplit -- the double_gyre experiment stepped with the UNSPLIT
! RK2 dynamics core instead of the default split RK2 + barotropic solver.
!
! MOM_input, MOM_memory.h, diag_table and input.nml are symlinks to
! ../double_gyre, so the two experiments cannot drift apart in anything but the
! overrides below.  Keep it that way: the coverage diff between them is only
! meaningful while the dynamics core is the sole difference.

! Drop the split time stepping and select RK2 (rather than the RK3 default)
! for the unsplit core.  USE_RK2 is only read when SPLIT is false, and it
! defaults to false, so it is load-bearing: without it this experiment would
! exercise MOM_dynamics_unsplit.F90 instead of MOM_dynamics_unsplit_RK2.F90.
#override SPLIT = False
#override USE_RK2 = True

! Required for stability, NOT a free choice.  With SPLIT = False there is no
! barotropic solver, so the external gravity wave (c = sqrt(GFS*H) =
! sqrt(0.98*2000) ~ 44 m/s) has to be resolved by the baroclinic step.  At this
! grid spacing (0.5 deg) that caps DT near ~600-700 s; double_gyre's DT = 1200
! blows up on model day 1 with "Excessive energy per unit mass forced model
! termination".  DT = 1200 and 900 abort; 600, 400, 300 and 200 complete.
!
! Consequence for the coverage diff against double_gyre: that comparison is not
! DT-matched, because no single DT is valid for both cores.  The dynamics
! signal dwarfs it, but a few percent of any global delta is the time step.
#override DT = 300.0
